## VERDICT
## **ACCEPT** 7.2 last-arg memory/perf honesty
SPRINT **7.2** (`c_sys_exec_last_arg` — no per-char OoStr concat / same
class as 7.1) is **true on source and on the live product host**:

1. **Source last-arg** (`ooda/oodac/c_emit_args.oo` `c_sys_exec_last_arg`):
   **zero** `out = out +` / `name = name +` / `last = last +`. Last span
   is **one** `str_slice(args, last_start, n)`.
2. **Host is not stale for the 7.2 body.** Product `ooda/oodac/oodac`
   (962960 B, md5 `a44ee35e…`, mtime 2026-08-12 07:49:59 -0700) **defines**
   `c_sys_exec_last_arg` and calls **`oo_str_slice` once, `oo_str_concat`
   zero times** in that function (objdump). Host mtime is **after** the
   slice land (HEAD already sliced). WT extras are **two comment lines**
   only (runtime auditor note).
3. **Long last-arg string is hang-free at 5s for reasonable size (≤4 KiB).**
   Isolated: 8 KiB **exceeds 5s** (~6.3s) on **println and ident-last
   too** — hang is **not** this extractor (lexer / string emit).

**Do not claim:** product emit O(n) or ≤5s for last-arg ≥8 KiB; 7.10
closed; `c_args_strip_cr` sliced; seed `bootstrap/seed/oodac` current.

**Do not REJECT 7.2** solely because WT grew two comments after host
build — 7.2 slice body is identical HEAD↔WT↔host.

