---
SOURCE (7.2 last-arg — live)
---

```
pub fn c_sys_exec_last_arg(args: String) -> String
  linear while i < chars_len(args)
  skip "..." (escape-aware), track paren depth
  top-level comma → last_start = next non-space
  let out = str_slice(args, last_start, n);   // ONE slice, not concat
```

Grep inside the function body (statements):

| Pattern | Hits |
|---------|------|
| `out = out + c` | **0** |
| `out = out +` | **0** |
| `name = name +` | **0** |
| `last = last +` | **0** |
| `str_slice(args, last_start, n)` | **1** |

Scanner still uses `char_at` (1-char `OoStr` per visit). That is the
language floor, not quadratic last-arg accumulate. Same class as 7.1.

**Same file L190** remains `c_args_strip_cr` `out = out + c` — **different
function** (8.6 CR strip).

